# Baseline for validate-verification-integrity.sh (W8-07).
#
# Format: <category>\t<repo-relative-file>\t<trimmed-line-text>
# (TAB-separated; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.)
#
# Each row is a specific line the validator would otherwise flag, reviewed
# and confirmed safe, with the reason recorded below. Keyed on line
# *content*, not line number: an unrelated edit elsewhere in the file does
# not invalidate a baseline row, but an edit to the flagged line itself
# does (it falls out of the baseline and must be re-reviewed) -- the
# validator does not silently keep suppressing text that has changed.

# apps/server/src/api/plans-routes.ts -- the POST /plan/evaluate route
# legitimately reads body.snapshot (W5-15/W5-16): it only matches the
# snapshot against the deterministic recommendation catalog (D-016) to
# create NEW `proposed` plan items. It never flips an item to done/verified
# from it -- that decision is made exclusively by verifyPlan's own
# server-derived snapshot (see the /plan/verify route right below it in the
# same file, which explicitly never reads body.snapshot). Two of these four
# rows are string-literal text inside an error message / doc comment, not
# executable reads, but are baselined too since the line-based scan can't
# tell the difference.
caller-input-state-flip	apps/server/src/api/plans-routes.ts	if (!isPlanEvaluationSnapshot(body?.snapshot)) {
caller-input-state-flip	apps/server/src/api/plans-routes.ts	badRequest(request, 'body.snapshot must be a full PlanEvaluationSnapshot'),
caller-input-state-flip	apps/server/src/api/plans-routes.ts	const { created } = await evaluatePlan(projectPath, body.snapshot);
caller-input-state-flip	apps/server/src/api/plans-routes.ts	* `body.snapshot` is never read: CLAUDE.md law 4 / SC-03 — an untrusted

# packages/tickets/src/reducer.ts -- the ticket.accepted case folds status
# to 'done' from an event that was already receipt-checked before it was
# ever appended: acceptTicket (packages/tickets/src/verbs.ts) refuses to
# emit ticket.accepted unless ticket.manifest.closeReceipt is present and
# the actor isn't the ticket owner (maker != verifier, FR-T2). The reducer
# is a pure fold over an already-validated event, not a fresh decision
# point, so there is no "receipt"/"anchor" text near this line to find --
# the check lives in a different file (verbs.ts), by design (events are the
# durable, receipt-checked source of truth; projections are disposable).
state-flip-no-anchor	packages/tickets/src/reducer.ts	status: 'done',
